Subject: [PATCH] docs: record patches 143 to 149 in the stack manifest

Phase P1 of the IndexedDB redesign: the database actor, each IndexedDB
transaction as one SQL transaction, the abort of a transaction whose
commit failed, the key generator in the backend with the key injected
when a value is read, the abort of a global's unfinished transactions
when it goes away, and the manager's metadata reads from the committed
metadata. The actor only changes fork files and is tier A; the other
five edit upstream files and are tier C; this bookkeeping entry is B,
like the earlier ones. The key generator entry no longer watches
key.rs, which it now changes, but the structured clone code that its
read-time injection relies on.

Validation: `uv run docs/ohos-sync/check_stack.py base/2026-11-09` passes.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
